    婆 | pó | grandmother; old woman
    叔 | shū | uncle; father's younger brother

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 外公 specifically designates one's mother's father in kinship terminology.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 外公 vs. 爷爷 | yéye | 外公 is maternal grandfather (mother's father), whereas 爷爷 is paternal grandfather (father's father).
    2 | 外公 vs. 姥爷 | lǎoye | 外公 is the standard, formal, and pan-Chinese written term for maternal grandfather, whereas 姥爷 is a colloquial dialectal term prevalent in northern China.
    3 | 外公 vs. 祖父 | zǔfù | 祖父 is the formal, literary designation strictly for the paternal grandfather, corresponding to 爷爷 in spoken register.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 除夕的午后，外公总会戴起老花镜，在暖阳下铺开红纸挥毫泼墨。他写下的春联墨香浓郁，苍劲有力的笔锋里凝聚着对儿孙平安顺遂的殷切期许，那抹喜庆的中国红，是童年里最温馨的年景。 | Chúxī de wǔhòu, wàigōng zǒng huì dài qǐ lǎohuājìng, zài nuǎnyáng xià pūkāi hóngzhǐ huīháo-pōmò. Tā xiěxià de chūnlián mòxiāng nóngyù, cāngjìn yǒulì de bǐfēng lǐ níngjù zhe duì érsūn píng'ān shùnsuì de yīnqiè qīxǔ, nà mǒ xǐqìng de Zhōngguó hóng, shì tóngnián lǐ zuì wēnxīn de niánjǐng. | On New Year's Eve afternoon, maternal grandfather would always put on reading glasses, spreading red paper in the warm sun to write calligraphy. His Spring Festival couplets carried rich ink fragrance, their vigorous strokes condensing earnest hopes for descendants' safety, the festive red remaining childhood's warmest memory. | En la tarde de nochevieja, el abuelo materno se ponía las gafas para escribir caligrafía sobre papel rojo al sol. Sus coplas festivas, impregnadas de aroma a tinta y trazos vigorosos, condensaban devotos augurios de dicha familiar, convirtiéndose en el recuerdo infantil más entrañable del año nuevo.
  #2 | 随着中国家庭代际结构的演变，外公外婆参与抚育第三代的比例在当代都市家庭中持续攀升。这种双系并重的代际照料模式，不仅有效缓解了青年双职工家庭的育儿压力，更促进了现代家庭关系的平等与和谐。 | Suízhe Zhōngguó jiātíng dàijì jiégòu de yǎnbiàn, wàigōng wàipó cānyù fǔyù dìsāndài de bǐlì zài dāngdài dūshì jiātíng zhōng chíxù pānshēng. Zhè zhǒng shuāngxì-bìngzhòng de dàijì zhàoliào móshì, bùjǐn yǒuxiào huǎnjiě le qīngnián shuāngzhígōng jiātíng de yù'ér yālì, gèng cùjìn le xiàndài jiātíng guānxì de píngděng yǔ héxié. | With the evolution of Chinese family intergenerational structures, the proportion of maternal grandparents participating in raising grandchildren has steadily climbed in urban households. This dual-lineage caregiving pattern eases childrearing pressures on working couples and fosters equality and harmony in contemporary family relationships. | La evolución demográfica china muestra un aumento constante de los abuelos maternos en la crianza de los nietos urbanos. Este cuidado compartido mitiga la carga de las parejas trabajadoras y favorece relaciones familiares más equitativas y armoniosas en la sociedad contemporánea.